. * Notes: one text, wrapped here into lines of at most 100 characters (PDF text runs wider than the PNG)
. local ntext "Notes: Firms are grouped once, by their `base_txt' records (in the group if so recorded in either year; n
> o record or answer = left out). ●~=~the group's change from `base_txt' to `post_yr' minus that of firms in the same in
> dustry and province, each firm against its own average (line = 95% interval; gray number: it includes 0, no clear diff
> erence). `post_yr' = the one later year whose energy records look normal. △~=~the same for `pre_txt': away from 0 = al
> ready moving apart before Paris (adopted December 2015). Counting only firms so recorded in every `base_txt' year they
>  answered, `sclr'~of~`sall'~● are clear, not~`nclr'. A shrinking group uses less energy: read with the value added and
>  workers rows. VA~=~value added = output value minus materials, energy and services bought, current prices. Table: `tr
> ans_yr' (transition), `all_rng' (Deasy's '2016+'), checks. Firm links are fictional: in `post_yr' only `still' of each
>  group's answering firms are still so recorded. Association, not the effect of Paris."

. local notelines ""

. local line ""

. foreach w of local ntext {
  2.     if ustrlen("`line' `w'") > 100 & "`line'" != "" {
  3.         local notelines `"`notelines' "`line'""'
  4.         local line "`w'"
  5.     }
  6.     else local line = strtrim("`line' `w'")
  7. }

. local notelines `"`notelines' "`line'""'

. * "~" keeps a number with its words on one line; it prints as a space
. local notelines : subinstr local notelines "~" " ", all

. display `"   note lines: `notelines'"'
   note lines:  "Notes: Firms are grouped once, by their 2013–14 records (in the group if so recorded in either year;" "
> no record or answer = left out). ● = the group's change from 2013–14 to 2018 minus that of firms in" "the same industr
> y and province, each firm against its own average (line = 95% interval; gray number:" "it includes 0, no clear differe
> nce). 2018 = the one later year whose energy records look normal." "△ = the same for 2010–12: away from 0 = already mo
> ving apart before Paris (adopted December 2015)." "Counting only firms so recorded in every 2013–14 year they answered
> , 16 of 51 ● are clear, not 10. A" "shrinking group uses less energy: read with the value added and workers rows. VA =
>  value added =" "output value minus materials, energy and services bought, current prices. Table: 2015 (transition)," 
> "2017–22 (Deasy's '2016+'), checks. Firm links are fictional: in 2018 only 39%, 71% and 15% of each" "group's answerin
> g firms are still so recorded. Association, not the effect of Paris."

